- "My 18 month old has started hand guiding over the past few weeks, he will do it to get us to unbuckle his highchair or open a bottle or hold something, he still points very regularly. A few people have mentioned kids with autism do the same thing, his doctor also said it could be loosely related. Does anyone else’s toddler do the same thing and be neurotypical? No looking for medical advice just other people’s experience" [sr054-0064]
- "I am worried he has apraxia of speech (CAS) and limb apraxia, or autism. My brother has level 3 severe autism and apraxia of speech. I have seen him communicate full sentences on a letter board but he is totally nonverbal otherwise. I am terrified of this same fate for my son. I’m terrified it’s in my genetics and I never should have had a baby. I love him so much it hurts. I’m glad he’s here but terrified of him having a difficult life and of going through the things i went through growing up all over again." [sr062-0054]
