- "I also admit that I do not always respect her fulness cues. When you’ve had a scare about weight gain, it is hard to shake the number of ounces you need to get in the day and just go with the flow. I find that I get extremely fixated on her taking in 24 ounces in a 24 hour period and while we don’t always meet that goal, I get extremely stressed when we are falling behind. This stress has led me to persist with a bottle feeding well past her giving signs that she’s done. In my defense, however she gives signs that she’s done after 1 ounce. I can’t feed her 24 times a day." [sr096-0083]
- "Has anyone dealt with a feeding aversion and overcome it? Do you have any tips or tricks or strategies for either my baby or me to get past this hurdle? It feels like a full-time job feeding this baby and I would like to enjoy her babyhood a little bit more rather than being so stressed out all the time. Between pumping and catching her at the perfect sleepy moment, I feel like we can’t leave the house or do anything. (for additional context this is my second baby. My first baby, who is now five, was exclusively breast-fed and took to it no problem.)" [sr096-0085]

